IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa17-helpers`

-- coa17-part21a-ch2-company.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 21A, Chapter 2 -- Information-gathering: the duties
-- on companies (ss 790CB to 790F; lines 10243-10350 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively. SOURCE, TARGET and
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER are as in coa17-part21-ch1.l4 (JUST TRUE: the text says yes; JUST FALSE: the text says no in its
-- own words; NOTHING: the text does not decide; a caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE).
--
-- THE GATE. Every duty here is a duty of "a company to which this Part applies" (s 790CB, 790D, 790DA, 790E, 790EA and, by
-- s 790B(1), the rest). Each function takes `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` (MAYBE BOOLEAN; the answer of
-- coa17-part21a-ch1.l4) and a JUST FALSE from it flows through, as the text's own no: "This Part applies to companies other
-- than ..." (fork F4); NOTHING stays NOTHING.
-- SEAMS. `s 1121 the officer is in default` (the offence in s 790F). Schedule 1B (another part's) is behind ss 790ED to 790EF.
-- TIME. "within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which X": the day itself counts, so the last day is
-- X plus 13. "by no later than the end of the period of one month beginning with the day on which it is given": the day before
-- the corresponding day next month (fork F2). Nothing reads today's date: a question that depends on "now" takes
-- `the day on which the question is asked`.
-- NOT ENCODED HERE (machinery, inert reason 2 in NOTES.md): the Secretary of State's regulation-making powers in
-- ss 790D(6)-(7), 790DA(7)-(8), 790E(5)-(6), 790EA(5)-(6).

-- FORKS in this module (NOTES.md, "Fork register (coa17)", gives each reading and the text that licenses it; the
-- coverage table points each row at its fork): F1 at s 790D(4), s 790E(4), s 790EA(4), s 790EB(2), s 790EC(2), s
-- 790ED(3), s 790EE(3), s 790EF(3); F2 at s 790D(3), s 790DA(5), s 790E(3), s 790EA(3); F5 at s 790CB, s 790D(2), s
-- 790D(4), s 790DA(4), s 790E(2), s 790E(4), s 790EA(2), s 790EA(4), s 790EB(1A), s 790EB(1B), s 790EC(1A), s
-- 790EC(1B), s 790ED(2), s 790EE(2), s 790EF(2); F7 at s 790EB(2); F8 at s 790DA(2); F9 at s 790D(4), s 790E(4), s
-- 790EA(4); F11 at s 790F(1); F19 at s 790DA(1).

§ `Part 21A Chapter 2: Information-gathering: duties on companies`

§§ `Duty to find out about persons with significant control (s 790CB)`

-- src:10246 | A company to which this Part applies must take reasonable steps to find out if there is anyone who is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company and, if so, to identify them.
@ref s 790CB Duty to find out about persons with significant control (src:10246)
GIVEN `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790CB the company must take reasonable steps to find out if there is anyone who is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity and, if so, to identify them` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company to which this Part applies" (a JUST FALSE from s 790B(1) flows through)
        (JUST TRUE)

@ref s 790CB must take reasonable steps (src:10246)
GIVEN `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the steps the company has taken are reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790CB the company has taken reasonable steps` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company`
        (IF `the steps the company has taken are reasonable steps`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must take reasonable steps" (a bare must not done: fork F5; whether the steps were reasonable is the person's plain input)

§§ `Company's duty to give notices to persons with significant control (s 790D)`

-- src:10258 | (5) A company is not required to give a notice under this section to a person if—
-- src:10259 | (a) the application for the registration of the company contained a statement of initial significant control naming the person as someone who would, on the company’s incorporation, become a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company, and
-- src:10260 | (b) the company has no cause to believe that at any time since its incorporation the person has ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company.
@ref s 790D(5) A company is not required to give a notice (src:10258-10260)
GIVEN `the application for registration of the company contained a statement of initial significant control naming the person as someone who would, on the company's incorporation, become a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has no cause to believe that at any time since its incorporation the person has ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790D(5) the company is not required to give a notice to the person under this section` MEANS
    IF    `the application for registration of the company contained a statement of initial significant control naming the person as someone who would, on the company's incorporation, become a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity`
       AND `the company has no cause to believe that at any time since its incorporation the person has ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is not required to give a notice under this section to a person if" (the if fails)

-- src:10248 | (1) A company to which this Part applies must give a notice to a person under this section if—
-- src:10249 | (a) the company knows or has cause to believe that the person is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company, but
-- src:10250 | (b) the company has not had confirmation of the person’s status as a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity or has not had confirmation of all of the required particulars of the person (see section 790K).
@ref s 790D(1) Company's duty to give notices to persons with significant control (src:10248-10250)
GIVEN `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company knows or has cause to believe that the person is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has had confirmation of the person's status as a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has had confirmation of all of the required particulars of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application for registration of the company contained a statement of initial significant control naming the person as someone who would, on the company's incorporation, become a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has no cause to believe that at any time since its incorporation the person has ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790D(1) the company must give a notice to the person` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company to which this Part applies" (a JUST FALSE from s 790B(1) flows through)
        (IF `s 790D(5) the company is not required to give a notice to the person under this section` `the application for registration of the company contained a statement of initial significant control naming the person as someone who would, on the company's incorporation, become a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity` `the company has no cause to believe that at any time since its incorporation the person has ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is not required to give a notice under this section to a person if" (subsection (5))
         ELSE IF    `the company knows or has cause to believe that the person is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company`
                AND (   (NOT `the company has had confirmation of the person's status as a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity`)
                     OR (NOT `the company has had confirmation of all of the required particulars of the person`))
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must give a notice to a person under this section if— (a) ... but (b) ..." (the if fails)

-- src:10251 | (2) The notice must require the person—
-- src:10252 | (a) to inform the company whether the person is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company, and
-- src:10253 | (b) if they are, to give the company all of the required particulars of the person (see section 790K).
@ref s 790D(2) The notice must require the person (src:10251-10253)
GIVEN `the notice requires the person to inform the company whether the person is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice requires the person, if they are, to give the company all of the required particulars of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790D(2) the notice requires what this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the notice requires the person to inform the company whether the person is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company`
       AND `the notice requires the person, if they are, to give the company all of the required particulars of the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must require the person— (a) ... and (b) ..." (a bare must not done: fork F5)

-- src:10254 | (3) The notice must require the person to whom it is given to comply with the notice by no later than the end of the period of one month beginning with the day on which it is given.
@ref s 790D(3) comply with the notice by no later than the end of the period of one month (src:10254)
GIVEN `the day on which the notice is given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790D(3) the last day for the person to comply with the notice` MEANS
    `s 790D(3) the last day of the period of one month beginning with the day` `the day on which the notice is given`

@ref s 790D(3) The notice must require the person to comply by no later than the end of the period (src:10254)
GIVEN `the day on which the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the day by which the notice requires compliance` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790D(3) the notice requires compliance within the period` MEANS
    `s 790D(3) the day required for compliance is no later than the end of the period of one month` `the day on which the notice is given` `the day by which the notice requires compliance`

-- src:10255 | (4) The company must give the notice—
-- src:10256 | (a) as soon as reasonably practicable after the company becomes subject to the duty to give a notice under this section, and
-- src:10257 | (b) in any event before the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company becomes so subject.
@ref s 790D(4) The company must give the notice as soon as reasonably practicable and in any event before the end of the period of 14 days (src:10255-10257)
GIVEN `the day on which the company becomes subject to the duty to give a notice under this section` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790D(4)(b) the last day for the company to give the notice` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the last day of the period of 14 days beginning with the day` `the day on which the company becomes subject to the duty to give a notice under this section`

@ref s 790D(4) the company has given the notice in time (src:10255-10257)
GIVEN `the day on which the company becomes subject to the duty to give a notice under this section` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the notice was given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the notice was given as soon as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790D(4) the company has given the notice in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 790D(4)(b) the act was done by the last day of the period` (`s 790D(4)(b) the last day for the company to give the notice` `the day on which the company becomes subject to the duty to give a notice under this section`) `the day on which the notice was given` `the day on which the question is asked` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any event before the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company becomes so subject"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the notice was given as soon as reasonably practicable`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as reasonably practicable after the company becomes subject to the duty"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not yet given, and the 14 days have not ended

§§ `Obtaining information from third parties (s 790DA)`

