      `the company knows or has cause to believe that the person knows the identity of someone likely to have that knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790DA(1) the company may give a notice to the person` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company to which this Part applies" (a JUST FALSE from s 790B(1) flows through)
        (IF    `the company knows or has cause to believe that the person knows the identity of someone who falls within subsection (2)`
            OR `the company knows or has cause to believe that the person knows the identity of someone likely to have that knowledge`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may give a notice to a person under this section if it knows or has cause to believe that the person— (a) ... or (b) ..." (the if fails: name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F19: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)

-- src:10267 | (2) The persons who fall within this subsection are—
-- src:10268 | (a) a registrable person in relation to the company;
-- src:10269 | (b) a relevant legal entity in relation to the company;
-- src:10270 | (c) an entity which would be a relevant legal entity in relation to the company but for the fact that section 790C(6)(b) does not apply in respect of it.
@ref s 790DA(2) The persons who fall within this subsection (src:10267-10270)
DECLARE `s 790DA(2) kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 790DA(2)(a) a registrable person in relation to the company`
    `s 790DA(2)(b) a relevant legal entity in relation to the company`
    `s 790DA(2)(c) an entity which would be a relevant legal entity in relation to the company but for the fact that section 790C(6)(b) does not apply in respect of it`
    `s 790DA(2) a person of none of those kinds`

GIVEN `the kind of person` IS A `s 790DA(2) kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790DA(2) the person falls within this subsection` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of person`
    WHEN `s 790DA(2) a person of none of those kinds` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The persons who fall within this subsection are— (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ..." (a list closed by "are", not "only": fork F8)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

