`s 790EF(1) the company must give notice to the registrar of the court's order` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part applies to companies other than" (a JUST FALSE from s 790B(1) flows through)
        (IF `a court makes an order under paragraph 8 of Schedule 1B directing that a relevant interest in the company cease to be subject to restrictions set out in a restrictions notice given by the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court makes an order under paragraph 8 of Schedule 1B ... the company must give notice to the registrar" (the where condition fails)

-- src:10337 | (2) The notice must state—
-- src:10338 | (a) that the court has made an order under paragraph 8 of Schedule 1B directing that a relevant interest in the company cease to be subject to restrictions in a restrictions notice, and
-- src:10339 | (b) the date of the order.
@ref s 790EF(2) The notice must state (src:10337-10339)
GIVEN `the notice states that the court has made an order under paragraph 8 of Schedule 1B directing that a relevant interest in the company cease to be subject to restrictions in a restrictions notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the date of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790EF(2) the notice states what this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice states that the court has made an order under paragraph 8 of Schedule 1B directing that a relevant interest in the company cease to be subject to restrictions in a restrictions notice` AND `the notice states the date of the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must state— (a) ... and (b) the date of the order" (a bare must not done: fork F5)

-- src:10340 | (3) The notice must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company is made aware of the court’s order.
@ref s 790EF(3) within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company is made aware of the court's order (src:10340)
GIVEN `the day on which the company is made aware of the court's order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790EF(3) the last day for the company to give the notice to the registrar` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the last day of the period of 14 days beginning with the day` `the day on which the company is made aware of the court's order`

@ref s 790EF(3) the notice was given to the registrar within the period (src:10340)
GIVEN `the day on which the company is made aware of the court's order` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the notice was given to the registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790EF(3) the notice was given to the registrar in time` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the act was done by the last day of the period` (`s 790EF(3) the last day for the company to give the notice to the registrar` `the day on which the company is made aware of the court's order`) `the day on which the notice was given to the registrar` `the day on which the question is asked` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company is made aware of the court’s order"

§§ `Failure by company to comply with information duties (s 790F)`

-- src:10342 | (1) If a company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with a duty under section 790CB, 790D, 790DA(3), 790E, 790EA, 790EB, 790EC, 790ED, 790EE or 790EF to take steps or give a notice, an offence is committed by—
-- src:10343 | (a) the company, and
-- src:10344 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 790F(1) If a company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with a duty ... an offence is committed (src:10342-10344)
DECLARE `s 790F(1) duty` IS ONE OF
    `s 790F(1) the duty under section 790CB`
    `s 790F(1) the duty under section 790D`
    `s 790F(1) the duty under section 790DA(3)`
    `s 790F(1) the duty under section 790E`
    `s 790F(1) the duty under section 790EA`
    `s 790F(1) the duty under section 790EB`
    `s 790F(1) the duty under section 790EC`
    `s 790F(1) the duty under section 790ED`
    `s 790F(1) the duty under section 790EE`
    `s 790F(1) the duty under section 790EF`
    `s 790F(1) another duty`

GIVEN `the duty` IS A `s 790F(1) duty`
      `the company fails to comply with the duty to take steps or give a notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790F(1)(a) an offence is committed by the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the duty`
    WHEN `s 790F(1) another duty` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a duty under section 790CB, 790D, 790DA(3), 790E, 790EA, 790EB, 790EC, 790ED, 790EE or 790EF"
    OTHERWISE
        IF (NOT `the company fails to comply with the duty to take steps or give a notice`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails ... to comply with a duty" (the if fails)
        ELSE IF `the company has a reasonable excuse`
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without reasonable excuse"
             ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 790F(1)(b) every officer of the company who is in default (src:10342-10344)
GIVEN `the answer under section 790F(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790F(1)(b) an offence is committed by the officer of the company who is in default` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold` `the answer under section 790F(1)(a)` `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:10345 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:10346 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:10347 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:10348 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or a fine (or both);
-- src:10349 | (ii) in Scotland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:10350 | (iii) in Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 790F(2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable (src:10345-10350)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 790F(2) the penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 2, unit IS Years)
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 12, unit IS Months)
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 12, unit IS Months)
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` WITH `fraction of the statutory maximum` IS 1)
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 6, unit IS Months)
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` WITH `fraction of the statutory maximum` IS 1)
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) on conviction on indictment, ... (b) on summary conviction— (i) in England and Wales, ... (ii) in Scotland, ... (iii) in Northern Ireland"
